@* The chips while the guide waits: the site's own questions at first, and once there is a talk, a next step from
   where it was. Each chip asks its question, one of them drawn bright, and the last word says the box is there too,
   since a chip is a shortcut and never the only way in (F134's rule 3). While they give way they stay drawn, stepped
   away and out of reach, so they ease out and back in. While the bar is closed they stand round its orb (FX173). *@
@if (Chips is { Questions.Count: > 0 } chips)
{
    <div class="@Classes" inert="@(!Show)">
        @foreach (string question in chips.Questions)
        {
            <button class="@(question == chips.Suggested ? "is-suggested" : null)" type="button"
                    @onclick="() => OnChoose.InvokeAsync(question)">@question</button>
        }
        <span class="agent-chips-note">@Text.OrTypeYourOwn</span>
    </div>
}
